  "interpretation": [
    "The matched frozen read protocol observed higher throughput and much lower read-copy wall cost/worker CPU in v26; bounded file integrity passed. This supports the cacheable payload implementation for further integration, not full stress or final firmware acceptance.",
    "v26 dma_start includes sync_device and post_reset includes sync_cpu; these are composite windows, not isolated cache-maintenance or reset cost. pre_reset nests inside dma_start; worker_total nests service/callback.",
    "The two runs differ in CPU endpoint distribution and background I/O. CPU frequencies/load/residency are not controlled; a single pair cannot establish a universal speedup or isolate each hardware cause.",
    "v26 aggregate read count/bytes equal the probe minimum, with background write activity. Equality is consistent coverage, not per-request identity proof. v25 has five surplus reads.",
    "Wall durations include interrupts/scheduling and are not directly measured phase CPU time. Worker CPU is tick-quantized, and dispatch crosses submission/worker execution contexts.",
    "Repeated8MiB prefix may hit device-internal cache; no unique-media sustained-throughput claim. Outer file path/inode/size match across runs, but the frozen probe embeds no target content hash.",
    "All lifetime maxima remain before/after values; no maxima were subtracted. Stable first-after counters are not a hardware drain."
  ],
